</figure>
<div id="S5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Given an input tuple <math id="S5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(N_{d},N_{A},\text{Extern})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mtext>Extern</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(N_{d},N_{A},\text{Extern})</annotation></semantics></math> for domain <math id="S5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{D}</annotation></semantics></math> in our dataset, we apply these four different methods to generate the corresponding PDDL domain <math id="S5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.
In total, we evaluate 30 domains, consisting of 14 simple (S.) domains and 16 complex (C.) domains as determined by <span id="S5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">domain complexity scores</span>, and we summarize these domain categories in Tab. <a href="#S5.T1" title="TABLE I ‣ V Evaluation ‣ SPAR: Scalable LLM-based PDDL Domain Generation for Aerial Robotics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">I</span></a>.
The domains are grouped into seven categories: Navigation (autonomous flight), Transportation (logistics), Manipulation (object interactions), Monitoring (assessment), Exploration (coverage), Aerial Operations, and Adaptation. Together, they span tasks from low-level control to high-level decision-making.
Note that for <span id="S5.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">FS</span> and <span id="S5.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ours</span>, which treat the dataset as an external source and retrieve examples from it, we explicitly exclude all information from domain <math id="S5.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{D}</annotation></semantics></math> itself to prevent bias.
As shown in Fig. <a href="#S2.F2" title="Fig. 2 ‣ II-C UAV Task Planning Benchmark ‣ II Related Work ‣ SPAR: Scalable LLM-based PDDL Domain Generation for Aerial Robotics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, after generating the domain, we evaluate it based on the number of syntax corrections, error types, problem-solving capability, and its overall feasibility and interpretability.</p>
</div>
